{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021576-psychic-powers-questions","id":1021576,"title":"Psychic powers questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-24T08:15:08-08:00","id":1021576,"title":"Psychic powers questions","content":"- Can Psychic Vampires (and other sub-templates) learn and use basic psychic powers from Chronicles of Darkness and Hurt Locker ?<br /> - Which psychic powers can Vampires learn with the Coil of Zirnitra ? I assume it goes without saying they would have unrestricted access to all psychic powers (and thaumaturgical abilities, but I am much less interested in them) from CoD and HL, but what about the sub-template powers from HL, such as the Psychic Vampire abilities ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T08:23:46-08:00","id":1021577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021576-psychic-powers-questions#post1021576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Can Psychic Vampires (and other sub-templates) learn and use basic psychic powers from Chronicles of Darkness and Hurt Locker ?<br /> - Which psychic powers can Vampires learn with the Coil of Zirnitra ? I assume it goes without saying they would have unrestricted access to all psychic powers (and thaumaturgical abilities, but I am much less interested in them) from CoD and HL, but what about the sub-template powers from HL, such as the Psychic Vampire abilities ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a reason that Psychic Vampires couldn't learn other Psychic powers.<br /> <br /> As for the Coil of Zirnitra, I don't think it was intended for vampires to acquire the powers of mini-templates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T12:42:57-08:00","id":1021648,"title":"","content":"The rule of thumb is:<br /> <br /> 1. Minor templates stack at ST discretion. If no reason to not, why not?<br /> <br /> 2. Supernatural Merits are roughly equivalent to minor templates in this.<br /> <br /> 3. Major templates don't stack with any other template. So a Vampire shouldn't get any merit or template intended for mortals.<br /> <br /> 4. When a mortal with supernatural templates takes upon a Major template, it is recommended for STs to apply the Sanctity of Merits in such a fashion to try and replicate previous lost powers with powers proper to the new template, up to and including the creation of new powers (disciplines or devotions, in this case) if deemed feasible and appropriate.<br /> <br /> Corollary: given the item 4, it can be assumed that any Major template should always translate powers to their native scheme, meaning that all templates and merits ate barred, but the development of equivalent powers is encouraged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T15:33:55-08:00","id":1021725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021576-psychic-powers-questions?p=1021648#post1021648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rule of thumb is:<br /> <br /> 3. Major templates don't stack with any other template. So a Vampire shouldn't get any merit or template intended for mortals.<br /> <br /> 4. When a mortal with supernatural templates takes upon a Major template, it is recommended for STs to apply the Sanctity of Merits in such a fashion to try and replicate previous lost powers with powers proper to the new template, up to and including the creation of new powers (disciplines or devotions, in this case) if deemed feasible and appropriate.<br /> <br /> Corollary: given the item 4, it can be assumed that any Major template should always translate powers to their native scheme, meaning that all templates and merits ate barred, but the development of equivalent powers is encouraged.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does this work in regards to Hunters, particularly those who are without Endowments to fall back upon? Hunters by and large don't even have a resistance stat against supernaturals, and even those with Endowments typically aren't terribly potent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T22:27:47-08:00","id":1021850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021576-psychic-powers-questions?p=1021725#post1021725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does this work in regards to Hunters, particularly those who are without Endowments to fall back upon? Hunters by and large don't even have a resistance stat against supernaturals, and even those with Endowments typically aren't terribly potent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters just work as mortals becoming supernatural here, as they are. We only could have some problems with Code changes in to other Integrity equivalents of supernatural, but we need first to know how Code will work in 2E with Integrity rules in first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T22:59:17-08:00","id":1021853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021576-psychic-powers-questions?p=1021850#post1021850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunters just work as mortals becoming supernatural here, as they are. We only could have some problems with Code changes in to other Integrity equivalents of supernatural, but we need first to know how Code will work in 2E with Integrity rules in first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, my apologies; I'd forgotten that Hunters were gaining new aspects in 2e...that or I somehow completely missed Code in 1e and have been a dumb this whole time.<br /> <br /> Either way, interesting stuff is going on, and thank you for answering my question. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T23:07:57-08:00","id":1021854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021576-psychic-powers-questions?p=1021725#post1021725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does this work in regards to Hunters, particularly those who are without Endowments to fall back upon? Hunters by and large don't even have a resistance stat against supernaturals, and even those with Endowments typically aren't terribly potent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a rather common mistake.<br /> <br /> Hunters are a game line. They are not, though, a template of any kind. By the rules above, you can argue that Endowments count as supernatural merits of their own, turning members of Conspiracies into minor templates, but that's all.<br /> <br /> For all intents and purposes, characters with minor templates are still &quot;mortals&quot; for those rules, even the ones who are actually immortals (minor template).<br /> <br /> Also, Hunter the Vigil is, though a game line, just intended on providing better rules for mortals who take up the Vigil, their current status being otherwise unadulterated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T23:58:25-08:00","id":1021869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021576-psychic-powers-questions?p=1021648#post1021648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rule of thumb is:<br /> <br /> 1. Minor templates stack at ST discretion. If no reason to not, why not?<br /> <br /> 2. Supernatural Merits are roughly equivalent to minor templates in this.<br /> <br /> 3. Major templates don't stack with any other template. So a Vampire shouldn't get any merit or template intended for mortals.<br /> <br /> 4. When a mortal with supernatural templates takes upon a Major template, it is recommended for STs to apply the Sanctity of Merits in such a fashion to try and replicate previous lost powers with powers proper to the new template, up to and including the creation of new powers (disciplines or devotions, in this case) if deemed feasible and appropriate.<br /> <br /> Corollary: given the item 4, it can be assumed that any Major template should always translate powers to their native scheme, meaning that all templates and merits ate barred, but the development of equivalent powers is encouraged.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is entirely irrelevant for the purposes of this discussion since the Coil of Zirnitra is purposefully and explictly meant to bypass these restrictions and allow Vampires to learn and use Supernatural Merits. It is the whole point of the Coil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T00:12:12-08:00","id":1021877,"title":"","content":"Actually it was, and there is nothing else to be said.<br /> <br /> To buy a Merit, you have to fulfill the requirements. Either the Kindred does, or not. If the Merit requires a template other than Vampire, so don't.<br /> <br /> I don't know how Psychic Vampire is right now, nor do I need. If it is a psychic merit, and your vampire can buy any psychic merit which he fulfills the requirements, then it's game. If it is first a template, or specifies any requirements a Vampire can't meet not even with this Coil, so no game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T00:36:20-08:00","id":1021888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021576-psychic-powers-questions?p=1021854#post1021854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a rather common mistake.<br /> <br /> Hunters are a game line. They are not, though, a template of any kind. By the rules above, you can argue that Endowments count as supernatural merits of their own, turning members of Conspiracies into minor templates, but that's all.<br /> <br /> For all intents and purposes, characters with minor templates are still &quot;mortals&quot; for those rules, even the ones who are actually immortals (minor template).<br /> <br /> Also, Hunter the Vigil is, though a game line, just intended on providing better rules for mortals who take up the Vigil, their current status being otherwise unadulterated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for enlightening me. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T03:30:01-08:00","id":1021921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021576-psychic-powers-questions?p=1021877#post1021877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it was, and there is nothing else to be said.<br /> <br /> To buy a Merit, you have to fulfill the requirements. Either the Kindred does, or not. If the Merit requires a template other than Vampire, so don't.<br /> <br /> I don't know how Psychic Vampire is right now, nor do I need. If it is a psychic merit, and your vampire can buy any psychic merit which he fulfills the requirements, then it's game. If it is first a template, or specifies any requirements a Vampire can't meet not even with this Coil, so no game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I do not see how this is any relevant to our topic. The Coil of Zirnitra is explictly and purposefully built to make an exception to all the normal template restrictions, and allow a Vampire that learns it to develop mortal Supernatural Merits, regardless of whether the character was a psychic or thaumaturge before she was Embraced or not. It makes psychic and thaumaturge powers vampiric abilities. If you have it, you fulfill the requirements to learn Supernatural Merits from Chronicles of Darkness and Hurt Locker, period, and all this template talk is pointless and distracting. The Coil also has a Scale that might even allow a vampire to learn some powers of other supernaturals (i.e. major templates) on a case-by-case basis, provided they are able and willing to indulge in some transplant mess. Admittedly, however, its intended use is a little more ambiguous than the clear-cut case of mortal Supernatural Merits. However, the relevant issue here is whether Psychic Vampire and other mini-template powers from Hurt Locker are also meant to qualify as Supernatural Merits for the purpose of this Coil, or not. I 'd be inclined to make the case at least for Psychic Vampire abilities, since they seem a specialized case of psychic powers much more than anything else.<br /> <br /> I do not take any stance on the Hunters tangent, since I strongly dislike the whole Van Helsing splat concept and I purposefully shunned it in both iterations of the WoD, despite my usual completist attitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 12-25-2016, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T07:48:01-08:00","id":1021980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021576-psychic-powers-questions#post1021576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Can Psychic Vampires (and other sub-templates) learn and use basic psychic powers from Chronicles of Darkness and Hurt Locker ?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure. Short of an ST call, the micro-templates are still mortals, and qualify.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Which psychic powers can Vampires learn with the Coil of Zirnitra ? I assume it goes without saying they would have unrestricted access to all psychic powers (and thaumaturgical abilities, but I am much less interested in them) from CoD and HL, but what about the sub-template powers from HL, such as the Psychic Vampire abilities ? </div> </div> </div> The micro-templates of Hurt Locker don't seem to be anything special. Well, not from a mechanical standpoint - the history, potential organization, story hooks and themes make them stand out in a way that regular psychic merits don't. But, from a purely mechanical standpoint, these are just a group of merits with a single merit as a prerequisit for other merits.<br /> <br /> Its not appropriate for Zirnitra to have access to all the merits, since they're not all psychic or magical in nature, or because the themes clash, but that's up to ST interpretation. But there's nothing stopping you from a mechanical perspective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Coil of Zirnitra is explictly and purposefully built to make an exception to all the normal template restrictions, and allow a Vampire that learns it to develop mortal Supernatural Merits, regardless of whether the character was a psychic or thaumaturge before she was Embraced or not. </div> </div> </div> Actually, I feel compelled to point out that, from a thematic standpoint, Zirnitra was developed to allow the reclamation of abilities / development of potential you had before your Embrace.<br /> <br /> &quot;Some Dragons have developed this Coil to regain the lost gifts granted to them by their heritage as part of a werewolf family. Some use it to recover the magics tied to their mortal bloodlines.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's seems to be a definite tie between your potential as a mortal and what you can do post-Zirnitra. Granted, this doesn't have much of an effect in gameplay, considering that STs that ban certain merits and the like are fairly rare, but it is a theme of the Coil to keep in mind. Still, this is why Zirnitra has a cautionary word on STs taking each merit into consideration before allowing them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have it, you fulfill the requirements to learn Supernatural Merits from Chronicles of Darkness and Hurt Locker, period, and all this template talk is pointless and distracting. </div> </div> </div> Psychic Vampire, Lost Boys, etc have been called &quot;micro-templates.&quot; Therefore, template discussion is relevant here because these micro-templates are in midsts of discussion.<br /> <br /> Not sure why you seem against this, though, because the general consensus is agreeing with your stance - Zirnitra vamps generally qualify for micro-templates, assuming they pass ST approval and fit the themes of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T09:52:44-08:00","id":1022018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021576-psychic-powers-questions?p=1021980#post1021980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sure. Short of an ST call, the micro-templates are still mortals, and qualify.<br /> <br /> The micro-templates of Hurt Locker don't seem to be anything special. Well, not from a mechanical standpoint - the history, potential organization, story hooks and themes make them stand out in a way that regular psychic merits don't. But, from a purely mechanical standpoint, these are just a group of merits with a single merit as a prerequisit for other merits.<br /> <br /> Its not appropriate for Zirnitra to have access to all the merits, since they're not all psychic or magical in nature, or because the themes clash, but that's up to ST interpretation. But there's nothing stopping you from a mechanical perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Full agreement here. I admit so far I made myself more familiar with HL Psychic Vampires and CoD psychic abilities than with thaumaturgical and 'undescript' Supernatural Merits and micro-templates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, I feel compelled to point out that, from a thematic standpoint, Zirnitra was developed to allow the reclamation of abilities / development of potential you had before your Embrace.<br /> <br /> &quot;Some Dragons have developed this Coil to regain the lost gifts granted to them by their heritage as part of a werewolf family. Some use it to recover the magics tied to their mortal bloodlines.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's seems to be a definite tie between your potential as a mortal and what you can do post-Zirnitra. Granted, this doesn't have much of an effect in gameplay, considering that STs that ban certain merits and the like are fairly rare, but it is a theme of the Coil to keep in mind. Still, this is why Zirnitra has a cautionary word on STs taking each merit into consideration before allowing them. </div> </div> </div>If you ask my firm opinion, a wish to recover lost potential for mortal supernatural abilities is where the Coil originally started, but it quickly evolved beyond that, and as things stand, the existence of any such pre-Embrace potential is no prerequisite whatsoever to unlock psychic or thaumaturgical powers with the Coil of Zirnitra. Dedication itself to develop the Coil as a Kindred provides all the necessary mystical potential, for whatever reason the vampire becomes interested in such things after the Embrace. Just like you don't need to have been a very life-oriented, sensual, or sun-liking guy to master the Coil of the Ascendant, or a very emotionally-controlled or violent mortal to master the Coil of the Wyrm. You may get interested in the kind of benefits the various Coils provide for reasons that only become evident after the Embrace, and the Coils work just as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Psychic Vampire, Lost Boys, etc have been called &quot;micro-templates.&quot; Therefore, template discussion is relevant here because these micro-templates are in midsts of discussion.<br /> <br /> Not sure why you seem against this, though, because the general consensus is agreeing with your stance - Zirnitra vamps generally qualify for micro-templates, assuming they pass ST approval and fit the themes of the game. </div> </div> </div>I just good irritated by seemingly insisted reference to general rules about no template stacking and mixing that the Coil is specifically written to bypass for mortal supernatural abilities. And for the reasons you posted, the 'micro-templates' are templates in name only.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}